From: Kali NetHunter rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rhodep: pin the USB and DSI rails at vendor voltage

Three more rails inherited from sm6375-sony-xperia-murray-pdx225.dts that sit
at their range floor because no consumer votes a voltage, the same mechanism
as the L9/L11/L24 fixes. None of these can corrupt storage, so they are
reliability rather than data-integrity, but each is below what the vendor asks
and the board's own tree names the right value.

	rail          sat at     vendor wants   feeds
	pm6125_l4     1104 mV     1232 mV        UFS PHY PLL, DSI vdda
	pm6125_l10    1624 mV     1800 mV        USB HS phy vdda18
	pmr735a_l7    2704 mV     3080 mV        USB HS phy vdda33

All three vendor values land exactly on the 8 mV grid, so there is no rounding
surprise. Pinning to min == max is what makes the framework vote them; the
vendor sets each with qcom,init-voltage in holi-regulators-pm6125.dtsi (L4A
1232000, L10A 1800000, L7E 3080000), which mainline has no equivalent for.

L4 is shared -- it is the UFS PHY PLL supply and the DSI vdda -- so raising it
touches the display. Both consumers want 1.232 V and it only goes up from
1.104 V, so it moves toward spec for both, but the display is the thing to
watch after flashing. L7's mainline max was Sony's 3544 mV; the vendor caps
L7E at 3300 mV, and pinning to the 3080 mV init keeps it well inside that.

A fix by inspection against the vendor tree, not yet measured on the rail.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -264,9 +264,16 @@
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * 1.232 V, not the 1104 mV the range floor gives. L4 is the
+		 * UFS PHY PLL supply and the DSI vdda; neither votes a voltage,
+		 * so the framework picks the minimum. The vendor pins it with
+		 * qcom,init-voltage = <1232000> (L4A). Shared rail: this moves
+		 * both the UFS PLL and the display toward spec.
+		 */
 		pm6125_l4: l4 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1100000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1300000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1232000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1232000>;
 		};
 
 		pm6125_l5: l5 {
@@ -295,9 +302,14 @@
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * 1.8 V, not the 1624 mV floor. L10 is the USB HS PHY vdda18;
+		 * the phy only enables it, so the framework picks the minimum.
+		 * The vendor pins it with qcom,init-voltage = <1800000> (L10A).
+		 */
 		pm6125_l10: l10 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1620000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1980000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 		};
 
 		pm6125_l11: l11 {
@@ -407,9 +420,15 @@
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <868000>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * 3.08 V, not the 2704 mV floor. L7 is the USB HS PHY vdda33;
+		 * the phy only enables it, so the framework picks the minimum.
+		 * The vendor pins it with qcom,init-voltage = <3080000> (L7E),
+		 * whose own max is 3300 mV.
+		 */
 		pmr735a_l7: l7 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <2700000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <3544000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3080000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3080000>;
 		};
 	};
 };
